# swing-stab.xrs - the sneak-kill thrust (VR-155): a thrust of the sword hand
# while crouched presses the attack; the same thrust standing does nothing; a
# reach to the floor is not a thrust.
#
# Needs the same as swing-edge.xrs: a loaded level in GAMEPLAY, GamepadOnly=0.
# Run:  .\tools\xrsim-run.ps1 -Path .\tools\xrsim\swing-stab.xrs
#
# What this can and cannot show. It shows the GESTURE: armed by the game's own
# crouch, recognised by extension, straightness and direction, and pressing the
# attack (HONOURED slash in a level with nobody to kill). Whether that attack
# becomes the stealth kill is the game's decision and needs an unaware guard in
# front: `swing: HONOURED kill` is the line, and it is the headset run's to get.
#
# The simulated head is at (0, 1.6, 0) facing -Z, so the modelled right shoulder
# is near (0.17, 1.38, 0.04). Thrusts go from a forearm in front of it straight
# out along -Z. The hand is only ever MOVED: a teleport is a tracking jump.

hand r to grip 0.20 1.25 -0.25 0 0 0 1200
@wait 1500
trigger r pull 300
@wait 2500
@mod swing on; swing mode edge; swing threshold 3.6; swing filter median; swing sword on; swing output rt
@mod swing stab on; swing stab arm sneak; swing stab speed 1.5; swing stab travel 0.20; swing stab ratio 0.75; swing stab forward 0.5
@wait 1000

# 1. Standing: the thrust is not armed, fires nothing and says nothing about it.
@mark
@modassert features.swing.stab.armed eq false
hand r to grip 0.20 1.25 -0.60 0 0 0 250
@wait 1200
@nolog (stab|swing): FIRE
hand r to grip 0.20 1.25 -0.25 0 0 0 1200
@wait 1500

# 2. Crouch (the game's own, B): the edge is logged once, then the same thrust fires
#    and the game starts an attack because of it.
@mark
btn b press 150
@log stab: ARMED - crouch 6s
@modassert features.swing.stab.armed eq true
hand r to grip 0.20 1.25 -0.60 0 0 0 250
@log stab: FIRE extension
@log swing: FIRE #\d+ stab
@log swing: HONOURED
@wait 1000
hand r to grip 0.20 1.25 -0.25 0 0 0 1200
@wait 1500

# 3. Still crouched: a short jab is rejected on travel, and the line says by how much.
@mark
hand r to grip 0.20 1.25 -0.37 0 0 0 120
@log stab: REJECTED travel
@nolog (stab|swing): FIRE
hand r to grip 0.20 1.25 -0.25 0 0 0 1200
@wait 1500

# 4. Still crouched: reaching down to the floor is not a thrust. 0.45 m in 450 ms
#    peaks near 1.9 m/s: fast enough to START a thrust, and rejected for not going
#    forward. (In 250 ms the same reach peaks at 3.65 m/s, which IS a slash.)
@mark
hand r to grip 0.20 0.80 -0.30 0 0 0 450
@wait 1400
@nolog (stab|swing): FIRE
hand r to grip 0.20 1.25 -0.25 0 0 0 1200
@wait 1500

# 5. Still crouched: a real slash is still a slash, once.
@mark
hand r to grip -0.40 1.10 -0.35 0 0 0 200
@log swing: FIRE #\d+ slash
@wait 1000
@nolog swing: FIRE #\d+ stab
hand r to grip 0.20 1.25 -0.25 0 0 0 1200
@wait 1500

# 6. Stand up again: disarmed, logged once.
@mark
btn b press 150
@log stab: DISARMED 6s
@modassert features.swing.stab.armed eq false

# 7. Three simulated thrusts through the real core, gates and arming. Standing,
#    so they must NOT fire; then armed for the test, they must.
@mark
@mod swing stab sim 2.2 200 3
@log swing: sim window finished: 0 fire 8s
@mod swing stab arm always
@mark
@mod swing stab sim 2.2 200 3
@log swing: sim window finished: 3 fire 8s
@mod swing stab arm sneak; swing stab off
